2026-09-27T03:28:06.4929606Z Description:
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4930165Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4930678Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4932224Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4933714Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4934016Z Update Note
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4934365Z ===========
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4934844Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4935204Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4935290Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4935537Z ================
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4935671Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4935833Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4936175Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4936374Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4936498Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4936766Z ====================================
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4936941Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4937085Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4937449Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4937775Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4938394Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4938892Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4939002Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4939406Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4939907Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4940169Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4940454Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4940837Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4940915Z Packages
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4941097Z ========
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4941218Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4942745Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4944071Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4944297Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4944749Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4945190Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4945741Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4946269Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4946678Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4946930Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4947310Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4947559Z ==========================
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4947696Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:06.4948744Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T03:28:06.5022251Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:06.5023382Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T03:28:06.5024764Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T03:28:06.5025098Z 
